        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "If Brief Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1767863855589",
            "false": "1767863893502"
          },
          "code": "IF_BRIEF_SUMMARY",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1767863788876",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767863788878_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_INPUT.$output.BriefSummary == 'Y'}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 Mini (Premium)",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Brief Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "BRIEF_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1767863855589",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767863855590_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input => {{$context.$nodes.GET_CONTACT_DETAILS.$output}} + {{$context.$nodes.GET_LEADS_DETAILS.$output}} + {{$context.$nodes.GET_OPTY_DETAILS.$output}} + {{$context.$nodes.REFINE_CALL_NOTES_OUTPUT.$output.result}} + {{$context.$nodes.REFINE_CONVERSATION_MESSAGES_OUTPUT.$output.result}} +  {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACTIVITY_DETAILS.$output }} + {{$context.$nodes.REFINE_NOTES_OUTPUT.$output.result }}\n\nFrom the above input follow below instructions to prepare a summary \n\nSummarization Rules\n\nFrom ContactRollup data:\n   - Identify if Contact is involved in Open Opportunities or Leads → \"KeyContact\".\n   - Identify if Contact is involved in Recently Won Deals → \"InfluentialContacts\".\nFrom Contact data:\n   - Derive from JobTitle and Affinity → \"DominantSeniorityLevel\"\n\n- Get the overall sentiments based on past engagements.\n    - Check for any concerns raised in the Past Engagement\n    - Identify if there are Open Opportunities or Leads\n    - Identify for any Positive factors like Product advocacy / service satisfaction etc from past engagements or feedbacks.\n    - Identify Key concerns, challenges, or negative feedback.\n    - Identify Key customer requirements or requests\n\nPrepare a Concise Summary (no more than 100 words section) - highlighting Profile, Influence on Opportunities/Leads and Engagement as below\n- Include Job title, functional role, seniority level, and location. if either of this is not available, don't mention about that. So let suppose Job title is not available , mention Role, seniority level, location etc. but not job title. Similarly if role is not available don't mention about that.\n- Mention any high-value, nearing-closure, or at-risk opportunities or leads the contact is involved in. STRICTLY Mention the Opportunity / Leads Name while summarizing.\n- Summarize open opportunities: total count, stages, overall status. STRICTLY Mention the Opportunity Name while summarizing.\n- Output snippet examples:\n   - \"John has 5 open opportunities totaling $xxx. Top 2 worth $yyy are on track to close next quarter.\"\n- If involved in recent lost deals, mention win/loss reason and comments. \n- ContactRollup.NumberOfOpenHotLeads is subset of ContactRollup.NumberOfOpenLeads So if ContactRollup.NumberOfOpenHotLeads = ContactRollup.NumberOfOpenLeads then that means all the Open Leads are Hot. No need to mention both in that case.\n- Output snippet examples:\n   - \"There are 5 open leads totaling $xxx. Top 2 deals worth $yyy are on track to close next quarter.\"\n- Mention the name of the contact wherever applicable, i.e. 'Lydia has * open leads' , Don't mention like 'The Contact has * open leads etc.'\n- Amount and Revenue should be preceeded with Currency Symbols like '$'. \n- Get the overall sentiments based on past engagements.  \n- Highlight any Concerns raised in the Past enagagement. \n- List out any Positive factors like Product advocacy/ service satisfaction from past engagement.\n\n\nDON'Ts\n- Do not mention keyword like 'Job-Title' , 'Jobtitle' , 'LastToucedDate' etc, instead mention logical readable words. \n- STRICTLY Don't mention \"Rollup\" word in the summary for e.g don't mention something like \"Contact Rollup shows .....\" instead mention as \"Lydia (PartyName) has * open hot leads, and Won opportunities .....\"\n- STRICTLY Don't mention statement like \"The contact has ......\" instead mention something like 'She/he has ..... '.  \n- STRICTLY Don't mention something like 'Noah influences opportunities' or 'Noah influences Leads' etc\n- STRICTLY Do not consider ContactRollup.NumberOfOpenCriticalServiceRequests and ContactRollup.NumberOfOpenServiceRequests while preparing Summary\n- STRICTLY Do not include PartyNumber, LeadNumber, or OpportunityNumber. Use contact name, Lead Name, or Opportunity Name instead.\n- STRICTLY Do not mention the IDs like StgId, instead go for logical name of stage\n- STRICTLY Do not use the Attribute names directly in summary like CallsMade, NumberOfTouches etc instead mention logical readable words. . \n- STRICTLY Don't mention about anything that is not present. So if Opty details are not there don't mention about that, similarly if no Jobtitle information available, don't mention about that etc.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT RULES: \n1. Do not include time part in the date fields and format should be MM/DD/YY.\n2. Do not include PartyNumber in the response, rather use contact names.\n\n\nStrictly follow below Format for Output\n\nFORMAT: \n\n- Return only the JSON object as specified below.\n- The \"Summary\" field must contain a compact HTML paragraph using only <p> tags; do not use <h1>, <h2>, <br>, extra line breaks, or newlines unless explicitly requested.\n- Write the summary in 4-5 concise sentences; include quantitative and factual details where available.\n- Do NOT use bullet points, numbering, or any recommendation language.\n- Each paragraph should be business-friendly, descriptive, and logically organized.\n- Mention values for Job Title, Location, Amount, Risk, etc., using <b></b> format.\n- Keep formatting minimal, structured, and clean; do not add spacing or blank lines between elements.\n\nStrictly follow this response format:\n\n{\n    \"<b>Summary</b>\": \"< You are a summarizer for contacts datasets. Output only paragraphs. No bullet points or numbered lists. Render each summary section using minimal, structured HTML in <p> tags only. Mention values like Job Title, Location, Amount, Risk, etc., within <b></b> format.>\"\n}\n\nImportant constraints  \n- Keep language concise, business-friendly.  \n\nTERMINATE"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 Mini (Premium)",
